  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper-level area of low pressure will\nmove eastward from Utah into Colorado this afternoon. High\ntemperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon\nwill be six to eight degrees below normal for this time of year. A\ntrough of low pressure will quickly move eastward across the\nforecast area Thursday. Nothing more than a few clouds will be\nassociated with this trough of low pressure. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will build northeastward across the\nSilver State Friday through Tuesday. A warming trend is expected\nthis weekend. By Sunday afternoon, maximum temperatures across\nNorthern and Central Nevada will be seven to nine degrees above\nnormal for this time of year. High temperatures will remain above\nseasonal values both Monday afternoon and Tuesday afternoon. Here\nare probabilities of maximum temperatures of 60 degrees or higher\nfor select locations in Northern and Central Nevada on Sunday,\nNovember 8th, 2026: \n\nOwyhee - 96%\nCarlin - 95%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nEly - 90%\nTonopah - 90%\nEureka - 90%\nElko - 85%\nWells - 85%\nJackpot - 80%\nSpring Creek - 75%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding unseasonably cool conditions this afternoon. High \nforecast confidence in a warming trend this weekend. High forecast\nconfidence regarding unseasonably warm conditions both Monday \nafternoon and Tuesday afternoon. Moderate forecast confidence in \ndry weather this afternoon through at least Tuesday. No deviations\nfrom the NBM model output.",
